  2026-11-25-address-form-open-ended-pin-state-check, "open-ended house/street + PIN must match the state"): the address
  form is asked after the parent has paid, so a blocked form leaves a paid order with no address (K-165), and the K-182
  iPhone test showed a house called "10" refused. validateAddress() changes in three places, and the same function still
  runs in the form and in the address route:
    line1   valid when non-empty after trim (was 5 or more characters); both messages and the 120 maximum are unchanged
    city    valid when non-empty after trim (was 2 or more); both messages and the 60 maximum are unchanged
    PIN     after the unchanged six-digit format check, an else-if: when the state is valid, the PIN's first three digits
            must belong to the picked state, else errors.pincode is exactly "This PIN code belongs to a different state.
            Please check your PIN code and state." (approved word for word). The table is the new, non-frozen
            src/lib/address/pin-state.ts (a new file inside this frozen folder would fail checkout-freeze); a prefix no
            state lists is unknown and always allowed, and a prefix shared by several states accepts all of them.
  One new import (pinMatchesState). Nothing else in the file changes: line2, state, the phone, name, email, age and terms
  checks, the types and the exports are the tag's. The frozen validate.test.ts follows by one literal (its own patch).

